# Explain after coding

After you write, change, or fix code, end the response by asking Michael if he wants an explanation of the code and how it works.

- Ask once, after the result. Do not explain the implementation unless he says yes.
- Skip the question when the turn did not change code.
- When he wants an explanation, show the code with the explanation. Cite the relevant lines in ```startLine:endLine:filepath blocks so each point sits next to the source it describes. Show enough of each piece to follow the flow. Do not paste whole files.
